DOCUMENT();
loadMacros("PGstandard.pl", "MathObjects.pl", "PGML.pl");
Context("Numeric");

BEGIN_PGML
Sequences

1. An arithmetic sequence has first term [`a_1 = -7`] and common difference [`d = -6`].
(a) Find [`a_{5}`]: [_____]{-31}
(b) Find the sum [`S_{5}`]: [_____]{-95}

Logic

2(a). Evaluate [`(r \to p) \to q`] when [`p = \mathsf{F}`], [`q = \mathsf{F}`] and [`r = \mathsf{T}`].
Enter 1 for true and 0 for false.[_____]{1}

2(b). Evaluate [`(q \land \neg r) \leftrightarrow \neg p`] when [`p = \mathsf{F}`], [`q = \mathsf{T}`] and [`r = \mathsf{F}`].
Enter 1 for true and 0 for false.[_____]{1}

2(c). Suppose [`p = \mathsf{F}`], [`q = \mathsf{T}`] and [`r = \mathsf{T}`]. What is the truth value of [`(q \lor \neg r) \to ((\neg q \lor p) \land r)`]?
Enter 1 for true and 0 for false.[_____]{0}
END_PGML
Context("Interval");
BEGIN_PGML
Linear algebra

3. Find the eigenvalues of [`A = \begin{pmatrix} 36 & 12 \\ -120 & -40 \end{pmatrix}`]. Enter the eigenvalues as a set, such as [`\{-1, 4\}`].[_____]{Compute("{-4, 0}")}
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
